id=v2507a_charge_boost
name=iQOO Z10 Turbo+ Charge Boost (V2507A)
version=3578
versionCode=35780
author=V2507A Native Adaptation
description=Native charging boost module for iQOO Z10 Turbo+ (V2507A / Dimensity 9400+ / MT6991): overrides DCHG_FCC via vfcs_class with 3 profiles, master current cap, dual-sensor thermal throttling, temporary pause, and one-tap stock restore.

[v3578: Native V2507A Adaptation + CPU Health Check Rework + IME Fix]
- Native V2507A channel: based on vfcs-core.ko disassembly, writing /sys/class/vfcs_class/fchg_fcc_ma triggers force_active_votable(DCHG_FCC, "VFCS_CLASS_EVENT"), bypassing thermal/FBON USER_FCC_EVENT limits (still bounded by kernel max_fcc=15600mA and adapter PDO safety clamp).
- Protocol gate & cgroup fixes: handles MTK missing /sys/fs/cgroup/unfrozen and static chg_protocol_support=0x3f behavior, preventing false cgroup errors and premature 5V triggers.
- Unit normalization: unifies instantaneous/lifetime/child CPU metrics to pct x 10000.
- Invalid-value handling: outputs -1 when unavailable/out-of-range and renders "-" in UI; shows "Idle in window" on 0 jiffies delta and "Insufficient sample" under 2 min uptime.
- IME input fix: skips validation and DOM rebuilds during IME composition.

[Hardware Facts (V2507A / MT6991)]
- DT current limit: 15600mA (vfcs/vivo,fchg-curr-max-ma; PPS 10000mA / UFCS 8000mA)
- DT tables: vfcs_cms/vivo,normal-tc-data-N (native steps: 15600/11720/9720/7720/6056 mA)
- Injection target: DCHG_FCC (via vfcs_class/fchg_fcc_ma force_active_votable)
- Effective target = min(segment_val, master_cap * thermal_scale (97/91/81/72/63%))

[Features]
- 3 profiles: Aggressive / Balanced / Stock
- Master current cap: defaults to 15600mA (native DT rating)
- 5-stage SOC current table: customizable per SOC range, flat by default
- Dual thermal protection: board 46.0~54.0C default (adjustable) + battery fixed 40.5~43.0C
- Temporary Pause / One-Tap Stock Restore (writes 0 to release VFCS_CLASS_EVENT)
- Log toggle & WebUI Health Check / Debug Log Export (/sdcard/Download)

[Safety]
Userspace sysfs writes only. Never modifies system partitions, never flashes, never remounts or bind-mounts. Uninstall or switch to Stock to hand control back cleanly.
